cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FMSL, please cite it as below."
title: "FMSL: exact fluid states of 0/0 points"
authors:
  - alias: "MJ Celedon"
version: 0.10.1
date-released: 2026-10-27
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23682015
repository-code: "https://github.com/dazbuddies-sketch/fmsl"
keywords:
  - multivariate limits
  - cluster set
  - Newton polygon
  - Puiseux series
  - real algebraic numbers
  - verified computation
abstract: >-
  FMSL computes, exactly, what a function does at a 0/0 point: the limit when it exists, and
  otherwise the full set of values it approaches (its fluid state, always a point, an arc or the
  whole circle R u {oo}), for rational functions of two and three variables, including
  denominators that vanish along curves. Results are cross-checked by independent algorithms.
